{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And they said: O El, Elohim of the spirits, etc.</b> He said the Name <b>El</b> because he saw the arousal of the intensification of the judgments, so he mentioned the quality of חסד אל (chesed of El) to sweeten the judgments." "And His saying <b>Elohim of the spirits for all flesh</b> — he advanced an argument that is acceptable before the Creator, for HaShem desires that all spirits accept His divinity upon themselves while they are yet in flesh in this world. And this is His saying <b>Elohim of the spirits</b> — meaning, 'the spirits' is an expression of thought and will, along the lines of what He said (Ezekiel 20:32) ״הָעוֹלָה עַל רוּחֲכֶם״. If so, even though the judgment He would execute to destroy them in an instant is a true judgment, as I have written the reason above — nevertheless, according to what appears in practice, it is that one man sins and upon the entire congregation You are wrathful, for the whole congregation is not in this sin, yet You put all of them to death; and from now on, Heaven forbid, the spirit would refuse such divinity." "<b>Further</b>, he intended to speak before Him words of appeasement that would be accepted before Him, according to what preceded him through knowledge of the degree of the desire that the Creator has. The first is the praise and hymn that the supernal host give Him; above that, the praise and hymn that the souls of the righteous give Him from the two treasuries of life: one treasury of souls that have not yet come into this world, concerning whom they said, of blessed memory (Yevamot 62a) ״until the souls in the body are exhausted״; and a second treasury of souls that have already come into this world and returned and were placed in the treasury of life. And all of them give song and praise and thanksgiving to the Creator, may His name be exalted, in the sod (Proverbs 16:4) ״כֹּל פָּעַל ה׳ לַמַּעֲנֵהוּ״. Above them is the song and praise that ascends from the souls that are in this world, who are within flesh, and it prevents them from knowing HaShem, yet they exert themselves to love HaShem and to praise Him and to give thanks to His utterance. This is supreme and cherished before the Creator above all, as the matters are explained at length in the Book of the Zohar and in the words of the Sages, of blessed memory." "<b>And for this reason</b> Moses acted wisely, and HaShem was appeased by the very thing that He desires, and he said <b>Elohim of the spirits for all flesh</b> — You desire that Your divinity be upon the spirits at the time they are in flesh, and if You put them to death You are lacking this desire; and it is not fitting to strengthen the judgments so that they bring about the loss of the acceptance of Your divinity by the spirits in flesh, which is the summit of Your ultimate desire." "And he said ״the man <b>one</b> sins״ — to say that according to strict justice they have no liability, for all of them did not sin so as to obligate them; rather, You are coming upon them in wrath, which is the intensification of the judgment, and this is what he said ״תִּקְצֹף״." "<b>האיש אחד יחטא.</b> It uses the future tense, because as yet he has not committed a sin for which he is liable to the death that is being consumed, for until now he has done only mockery, and if he had repented there would be no obligation upon him."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:29.536250133Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}